    "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
    "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear"
  ],
  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "direct judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The principal scope objection is sustained independently: the theorem establishes properties of a prescribed scalar moving step, whereas the selected passage discusses discontinuous conservation-law solutions in the inherited vector-valued, potentially nonlinear setting. An illustrative witness does not establish that general comparison.",
      "primary_evidence": "Raw page 23 introduces q with values in R^m; raw page 26 discusses nonlinear fluxes; raw page 27 states the comparison without prescribing a profile. The elaborated target fixes Real, identity flux, and timeShiftedStep v 1."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "The blind translation correctly reconstructs the target's three conjuncts and parameter scope. Its identification of the integration measure remains conditional; this is an evidence limitation rather than evidence of an incorrect measure.",
      "primary_evidence": "D001–D007 reconstruct q_v(x,t) = h_v(x−(t−1)), rectangle conservation, and classical failure at (0,1). D020 and the final target conjunct assert absence of a mass derivative at time 1. D052 displays only inferInstance."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined with acceptance false: Lean-implies-source is definitively no, while the reverse direction is not certified from the allowed evidence. The definite specialization defect already excludes both accepted classifications.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target universally quantifies only the jump representative v, not the state dimension, flux, solution, or discontinuity point. The supplied methodology requires preserving an unresolved implication rather than forcing a binary classification."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "Retain undetermined for the same independently checked implication pair. Agreement between judges is not the justification; the target's explicit specialization and the unresolved source interpretation are.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind dossier and direct dossier have matching target structure after replacing LocalDef001–LocalDef007 by their supplied names. Raw pages 26–27 do not define the temporal or trace conventions for discontinuous solutions."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D052 unclear",
      "resolution": "The supplied declaration identifies a fixed library measure-space instance, but does not expose its selected measure or normalization. D025 merely projects that instance's measure. The direct judge's unconditional identification with ordinary dx and dt is not established by these displayed bodies. Preserve this narrow uncertainty.",
      "primary_evidence": "D052 has type MeasureTheory.MeasureSpace Real and body inferInstance. D025 has body fun α self => self.2. No supplied reuse entry certifies D052's measure identity."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D002 unclear",
      "resolution": "The declaration meaning is settled: D002 asserts spatial-slice integrability, temporal endpoint-flux integrability, and conservation integrated over time for every oriented rectangle. It contains no mass-derivative assertion. Its equivalence to an everywhere ordinary-derivative reading of (1.10) is definitively false; correspondence with the source's informal discontinuous interpretation remains unspecified.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 equates M_ab(t)−M_ab(s) with the temporal integral of f(q(a,τ))−f(q(b,τ)). Raw page 26 displays M_ab'(t) = f(q(a,t))−f(q(b,t)). The target's third conjunct denies every derivative of M_01 at time 1."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D020 unclear",
      "resolution": "HasDerivAt is understood as an ordinary two-sided derivative here. Its use in the classical predicate is appropriate. Its final negation concerns a different function, spatial mass as a function of time, and therefore adds a distinct assertion. The uncertainty concerns source correspondence, not the derivative operator's meaning.",
      "primary_evidence": "D020 uses the neighborhood filter at the point with a fixed base point. The explicit target instantiates the standard real metric and topology. D001 differentiates q's coordinate slices; the third conjunct differentiates an interval integral."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left dependency_coverage item D040 unclear",
      "resolution": "Negation has its ordinary logical meaning and the intended polarity. Negating D001 denies the joint existence of derivative witnesses satisfying the equation; it does not syntactically assert failure of each derivative separately. The explicit step nevertheless has unequal one-sided spatial limits, so its classical failure is substantive.",
      "primary_evidence": "D040 is fun a => a → False. D001 is an existential conjunction. D003, D005, D006, and D007 give q_v(x,1) = 0 for x < 0 and 1 for x > 0, independently of v."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "There is no impossible smoothness premise or assumption that arbitrary discontinuous functions conserve. The target instead fixes its entire solution family by construction, which reduces applicability. Its all-slice integrability requirements are explicit conclusions. Their identification with a general source solution class remains unspecified.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target has no propositional hypotheses on v. D002 includes integrability as conjuncts. Raw page 26 assigns sufficient smoothness to deriving the differential equation, while raw page 27 discusses discontinuous conservation-law solutions."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The local definitions, arithmetic, flux orientation, derivative operator, and logical connectives are understood. The rectangle balance is a substantive temporal reformulation, not an unfolding of the displayed derivative identity. The only unresolved dependency interpretation singled out by the supplied evidence is D052's measure identification.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002, D069, and D083 specify oriented integrals and integrability; D067 fixes identity flux; D082 and D093 preserve subtraction signs. D020 and D040 specify differentiation and negation. D052 stops at inferInstance."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The endpoint-crossing issue is genuine. Conditional on ordinary Lebesgue integration, M_01(t) equals 1 for t ≤ 1, 2−t for 1 ≤ t ≤ 2, and 0 for t ≥ 2. Its one-sided slopes at 1 are 0 and −1 for every v. No choice of jump value restores an ordinary derivative there. The source's treatment of such exceptional times remains unstated.",
      "primary_evidence": "The piecewise formula follows directly by integrating the function specified by D003–D007 over 0..1, with singleton values ignored under Lebesgue measure. Raw page 26 displays (1.10), and raw page 27 extends integral validity without an exceptional-time convention."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target is an explicit example, with no uniqueness, entropy admissibility, or formation-from-smooth-data assertion. Its integrability and rectangle identity are precise, but the selected introductory pages do not identify this exact solution class. Preserve that source-level uncertainty without inventing missing hypotheses.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 supplies only slice integrability and rectangle balance. The target contains no general solution binder. Raw page 27 refers shock-solution theory to Chapter 11."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The translated operators agree with the supplied declarations. The measure concern cannot be discharged by declaration naming, module ownership, or the direct judge's assurance. It remains an unverified identification, not a demonstrated semantic substitution.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind and direct dossiers both give D052 as inferInstance and D025 as measure projection. D069 explicitly uses that projected measure in both oriented interval integrals."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Exact equality and left-minus-right flux are preserved. Equivalence with an everywhere derivative law is ruled out by the target's third conjunct. An integrated-in-time interpretation can accommodate that conjunct, but the selected pages do not choose it explicitly. The additional conjunct cannot make a restricted example faithful-stronger.",
      "primary_evidence": "D002 preserves the flux difference and exact equality; D014 conjoins all three claims. Equation (1.10) displays a derivative, and the final target conjunct denies such a derivative for one interval and time."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "Equal and reversed endpoints are handled by the oriented integral definition, and the jump representative is universally unrestricted. Under Lebesgue integration, that representative affects only isolated points in spatial or fixed-position temporal slices. These facts explain the example's consistency but do not supply the source's missing endpoint convention.",
      "primary_evidence": "D069 subtracts integrals over (a,b] and (b,a]; D083 requires integrability on both. D006 selects v only at equality, and D003–D007 place that equality at x = t−1."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The example's intended nonvacuity is confirmed: v ranges over an inhabited real type, the states 0 and 1 remain distinct, and no assumptions exclude the jump. With ordinary Lebesgue integration its bounded slices are integrable and its mass changes nontrivially. Certification of the exact measure and of correspondence to the source's informal solution notion remains separate.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target is unconditional for every v. D006 fixes distinct one-sided states. D002 includes integrability, preventing reliance solely on totalized integral values outside their intended domain."
    },
    {
      "item": "direct judge left implication source_implies_lean unclear",
      "resolution": "The reverse implication remains uncertified. The source's classical-failure assertion can be applied only after identifying the constructed object as a solution in the relevant sense. These pages do not fix that sense at endpoint-crossing times or assert the additional mass-nondifferentiability conclusion. An independent elementary verification under Lebesgue integration establishes a useful example, but does not by itself settle statement correspondence.",
      "primary_evidence": "Raw page 23 gives translated advection profiles; raw pages 26–27 give the informal integral/classical comparison. The target additionally asserts D002's exact rectangle formulation and universal denial of the mass derivative at time 1."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "The same uncertainty applies to the translation, which accurately preserves the target's extra conclusion and restricted family. There is no translation error that would resolve the reverse implication differently from the direct comparison.",
      "primary_evidence": "The blind translation reconstructs q_v, every rectangle endpoint quantifier, classical failure at (0,1), and absence of every derivative of M_01 at 1. Each is present in the elaborated target and D001–D007."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "no",
      "reasoning": "The target gives one scalar unit-speed step family with identity flux and classical failure at one designated point. It does not establish the selected comparison for general vector-valued, potentially nonlinear conservation-law solutions. Even granting ordinary Lebesgue measure and a favorable integrated-in-time interpretation of the source, this scope reduction remains. Under an everywhere ordinary-derivative reading of (1.10), the target additionally denies the required derivative for its chosen interval at time 1."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "unclear",
      "reasoning": "The supplied source supports the relevance of translated advection profiles and continued integral validity for discontinuous solutions, but leaves temporal and endpoint conventions unspecified. It does not explicitly identify D002's precise rectangle formulation or assert the extra mass-nondifferentiability conclusion. The displayed D052 evidence also does not certify the integration measure's identity. Under the conventional Lebesgue and integrated-in-time interpretation, the example's claims can be independently verified, but that conditional verification does not resolve the exact source-to-target correspondence."
    }
  },
  "classification": "undetermined",
  "accepted": false,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The selected primary-source pages do not specify whether continued validity of (1.10) means an almost-everywhere derivative identity, an integrated-in-time balance, or a statement subject to endpoint trace conventions.",
    "D052's displayed body does not expose the inferred measure-space instance sufficiently to certify its measure identity and normalization from the permitted declaration evidence.",
    "Consequently, source-implies-Lean remains uncertified, although the missing general source scope definitively excludes acceptance."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "restricted-applicability",
      "evidence": "Raw pages 23 and 26 provide vector-valued states and linear or nonlinear fluxes. The elaborated target fixes Real, identity flux, states 0 and 1, speed 1, shift 1, and classical failure at (0,1).",
      "impact": "The theorem is an illustrative specialization. Generic signatures of imported definitions and an extra conclusion do not restore the general selected comparison."
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "category": "temporal-formulation",
      "evidence": "Equation (1.10) differentiates spatial mass. D002 integrates endpoint flux over time, while the target's third conjunct denies every ordinary mass derivative at time 1.",
      "impact": "An everywhere derivative interpretation is incompatible with this target. A weaker temporal interpretation is mathematically plausible but not specified by the selected pages."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "category": "dependency-evidence-gap",
      "evidence": "D052 displays inferInstance; D025 only projects its measure. The supplied reuse ledger does not resolve D052.",
      "impact": "Identification with ordinary Lebesgue integration remains conditional. This is not evidence that the actual library instance is incorrect."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "additional-conclusion-and-nonvacuity",
      "evidence": "The target unconditionally asserts a mass-derivative failure for every real jump representative. D003–D007 specify unequal one-sided states; under Lebesgue integration the unit-interval mass has slopes 0 and −1 at the crossing.",
      "impact": "The example has substantive mathematical content and no impossible premise. Its extra diagnostic is distinct from classical PDE failure and cannot establish overall faithful strength."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "The attached primary-source images, both dossiers, dependency inventory and reuse records, blind translation, judgments, and exact triggers were inspected without tools or reliance on target proof. Supplied hashes were treated as provenance, not independently recomputed. Declaration meaning was separated from source correspondence: differentiation and negation are clear, rectangle balance differs from an everywhere derivative law, and the measure identification remains insufficiently exposed. The source's general scope is definitely absent from the target. Because the reverse implication remains unresolved, the classification is undetermined with acceptance false; neither agreement among judges nor the example's mathematical usefulness supplies missing semantic evidence."
}
